import Mathlib

/-!
# The arm-multiplicity layer of the K58 (15,14,14,14) profile

Kernel-checked part of the profile enumeration: the arithmetic filter that
leaves 48 multiplicity profiles, and a witness for each of the 44 that survive
the incidence layer.  The other four are refuted by DRAT (see REPORT.md).

A *profile* of an ordinary 14-arm is the multiset of multiplicities of its zero
sets `Z(v)` (the classes of equal `Z(v)`).  With `c_j` the number of classes of
multiplicity `j`, the campaign-established exclusions are

  X1  multiplicity at most five,
  X2  at most one class of multiplicity five,   `c5 <= 1`;
  X3  a class of multiplicity five forces every other multiplicity at most
      three, so `c5 = 1` implies `c4 = 0`;
  X4  at least six distinct classes,   `6 <= c1+c2+c3+c4+c5`;
  X5  no three classes of multiplicity four,  `c4 <= 2`
      (redundant given X4, see `x5_redundant`);

together with `sum_j j*c_j = 14`, because the arm has 14 vertices.

`arith_filter` says those conditions force one of the 48 count vectors of
`cand`.  `witnesses` says each of the 44 vectors that survive the incidence
layer has an explicit family of 5-subsets of `Fin 15` with weighted point totals
all equal to 4 or 5.
-/

open Finset

namespace K58

/-- One class: a multiplicity and its support in `A = Fin 15`. -/
abbrev Cls := ℕ × Finset (Fin 15)

/-- The incidence conditions of one ordinary arm, as a decidable test: the
supports are distinct 5-subsets of the 15 points and every point has weighted
total 4 or 5 (it is seen in colour `0` by 4 or 5 arm vertices). -/
def Good (data : List Cls) : Bool :=
  ((data.map Prod.snd).eraseDups.length == data.length) &&
    data.all (fun p => p.2.card == 5) &&
    (List.finRange 15).all (fun a =>
      let t := (data.map (fun p => if a ∈ p.2 then p.1 else 0)).sum
      t == 4 || t == 5)

/-- The profile of a witness: the list of its multiplicities. -/
def profile (data : List Cls) : List ℕ := data.map Prod.fst

/-! ## The arithmetic filter -/

